---
---

<section id="how-it-works" class="section-spacing border-b border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--surface-tint)]">
  <div class="site-container">
    
    <!-- Asymmetric 2-Column Split matching mock.png -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12 items-start">
      
      <!-- Left Column: Story Headline, Narrative & Read Full Story CTA (lg:col-span-4) -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-4 flex flex-col justify-start">
        <div class="text-xs font-mono font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-[var(--brand)] mb-3">
          A PERSONAL STORY
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-[var(--ink)] tracking-tight mb-4">
          My journey to MastiDB
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          MastiDB started as a learning project — a way for me to truly understand how modern analytical databases work. Along the way it turned into a real, working engine.
        </p>

        <!-- Read full story button matching mock -->
        <div>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/lokeshdevnani/mastidb/blob/main/ARCHITECTURE.md"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-3 rounded-xl border border-[var(--line)] bg-[var(--surface)] hover:bg-[var(--lavender)] text-xs font-semibold text-[var(--ink)] hover:text-[var(--brand)] hover:border-[var(--brand)]/30 transition-all shadow-xs"
          >
            <span>Read the full story</span>
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-[var(--brand)]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3" />
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right Column: Connected 3-Step Horizontal Timeline with Custom Graphics (lg:col-span-8) -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-8">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 relative">
          
          <!-- Step 1: Druid -->
          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--surface)] border border-[var(--line)] shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between relative group hover:border-[var(--brand)]/40 transition-all">
            <div>
              <!-- Number badge and arrow on desktop -->
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[var(--brand)] text-white font-mono font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs">
                  1
                </div>
                <!-- Connecting arrow pointing right to step 2 (visible on md+) -->
                <div class="hidden md:block text-[var(--brand)]/40 text-lg select-none font-bold">
                  →
                </div>
              </div>

              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--ink)] mb-2">
                Druid
              </h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
                I first worked with Apache Druid at Udaan and Percept Insight and was fascinated by how it could query huge datasets so quickly.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Database Cylinder Graphic matching mock -->
            <div class="flex items-center justify-center pt-2">
              <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--surface-tint)] border border-[var(--line)] flex flex-col items-center justify-center p-2 group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform">
                <!-- Stacked database cylinders -->
                <div class="w-8 h-3 rounded-full bg-[var(--brand-blue)]/30 border border-[var(--brand-blue)] mb-1"></div>
                <div class="w-8 h-3 rounded-full bg-[var(--brand-blue)]/50 border border-[var(--brand-blue)] mb-1"></div>
                <div class="w-8 h-3 rounded-full bg-[var(--brand-blue)] border border-[var(--brand-blue)]"></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 2: Database Systems -->
          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--surface)] border border-[var(--line)] shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between relative group hover:border-[var(--brand)]/40 transition-all">
            <div>
              <!-- Number badge and arrow on desktop -->
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[var(--brand)] text-white font-mono font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs">
                  2
                </div>
                <!-- Connecting arrow pointing right to step 3 (visible on md+) -->
                <div class="hidden md:block text-[var(--brand)]/40 text-lg select-none font-bold">
                  →
                </div>
              </div>

              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--ink)] mb-2">
                Database courses
              </h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
                That curiosity led me to delve deeper through database courses, papers and open source columnar storage systems.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Open Book / Papers Graphic matching mock -->
            <div class="flex items-center justify-center pt-2">
              <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--surface-tint)] border border-[var(--line)] flex items-center justify-center p-2 group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform">
                <svg class="w-8 h-8 text-[var(--dict-violet)]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 6.253v13m0-13C10.832 5.477 9.246 5 7.5 5S4.168 5.477 3 6.253v13C4.168 18.477 5.754 18 7.5 18s3.332.477 4.5 1.253m0-13C13.168 5.477 14.754 5 16.5 5c1.747 0 3.332.477 4.5 1.253v13C19.832 18.477 18.247 18 16.5 18c-1.746 0-3.332.477-4.5 1.253" />
                </svg>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 3: Building MastiDB -->
          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--surface)] border border-[var(--line)] shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between relative group hover:border-[var(--brand)]/40 transition-all">
            <div>
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
                <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[var(--brand)] text-white font-mono font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center shadow-xs">
                  3
                </div>
              </div>

              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[var(--ink)] mb-2">
                Building MastiDB
              </h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-[var(--muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
                So I built MastiDB — a small, from-scratch OLAP engine in Python to make these architectural ideas concrete.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Mascot Logo Avatar Graphic matching mock -->
            <div class="flex items-center justify-center pt-2">
              <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--lavender)] border border-[var(--brand)]/20 flex items-center justify-center p-2 group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform">
                <img src="/mastidb-logo.png" alt="MastiDB Character" class="w-10 h-10 object-contain" />
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>
